    <era:status>unknown</era:status>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Cellulase treatment is a feed processing method that involves applying cellulase enzymes to raw feed materials before animal consumption. This enzymatic process breaks down cellulose present in plant-based feeds into simpler, more digestible components, thereby improving nutrient availability and overall feed quality. (HV GPT4)</skos:definition>
