  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/era-aom/livestock/AOM_000240">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Dry matter is calculated as the difference between the total weight and the moisture content. It is usually obtained by oven-drying, but there are methods specific to products such as silages, fats and molasses. Usually abbreviated as DM. Source: Feedipedia</skos:definition>
