    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Koronivia grass (Brachiaria humidicola (Rendle) Schweick) is a tropical grass from East and South-East Africa and was introduced to Australia, the Pacific Islands and South America. It is an important pasture in the humid tropics (Cook et al., 2005; Schultze-Kraft et al., 1992). [Feedipedia]</skos:definition>
