    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A control or reference diet serves as the standard or baseline nutritional plan against which the effects of modified or experimental diets are compared. This diet typically reflects the current or commonly used feeding practices for a specific animal species, growth stage, or production goal. (HV GPT4)</skos:definition>
