  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/era-aom/livestock/AOM_000828">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Direct boiling involves placing the feed directly in boiling water for a certain period of time to improve its digestibility and reduce anti-nutritional factors. This process is typically used for small-scale feed processing, such as for backyard poultry or pigs. (Human validated chatGPT).</skos:definition>
