    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Feeds added to animal diets that come from non-woody crops usually grown for human consumption. These can be crop grain, field residues (for example maize stalks left over once the grain component has been harvested), or processing residues (for example the maize bran produced as a byproduct of milling flour). Soyabeans fit in this category as they are grown for human consumption and livestock feed.</skos:definition>
