  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/era-aom/livestock/AOM_000104">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Gamba grass (Andropogon gayanus Kunth) is a perennial leafy grass of tropical Africa. Highly productive, drought- and fire-resistant grass, it forms dense stands used for pastures, hay and cut-and-carry systems. It is relished by livestock when young (before heading) and loses its nutritional value when it matures. [Feedipedia]</skos:definition>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Tambuki Grass</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Rhodesian Blue Grass</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Andropogon bisquamulatus</skos:altLabel>
